{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/23158","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:56:05.778480+00:00","comments":[],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"NONE","body":"### What happened?\n\n## Description\n\nWhen compiling StableHLO with `--iree-opt-const-eval=true`, compilation fails with a runtime error during constant evaluation.\n\n## Error Message\n\n<unknown>:0: error: runtime error in consteval: iree/runtime/src/iree/hal/drivers/local_task/task_device.c:72: INVALID_ARGUMENT; must have at least one queue\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce your issue\n\n1. Compile attached StableHLO file with:\n   ```bash\n   iree-compile --iree-input-type=stablehlo \\\n     --iree-hal-target-device=cuda \\\n     --iree-cuda-target=sm_80 \\\n     --iree-opt-const-eval=true \\\n     jax_ir0001_jit_graupel_run_compile.mlir \\\n     -o output.vmfb\n\n[jax_ir0001_jit_graupel_run_compile.mlir.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24655881/jax_ir0001_jit_graupel_run_compile.mlir.txt)\n\n### What component(s) does this issue relate to?\n\n_No response_\n\n### Version information\n\niree v3.9.0 and main branch\n\n### Additional context\n\nWorkaround:\nUsing --iree-opt-const-eval=false allows compilation to succeed, but disables the optimization.","closed_at":null,"closed_by":null,"comments":0,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/23158/comments","created_at":"2026-01-15T23:15:02Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/23158/events","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/23158","id":3819585736,"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"total_blocking":0},"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"d73a4a","default":false,"description":"Something isn't working","id":1553038945,"name":"bug 🐞","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNTUzMDM4OTQ1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/lab